<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="a3a4eea0"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="86ae021f">The handover plan should be developed through detailed discussion with the Benefit Sponsor and the BAU function that is
taking responsibility for on-going tracking. It may be necessary to hold a series of planning sessions to review the status
of each benefit, and how it will be handled when the program closes.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="d980d1d3"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="4e0cdb15">&lt;p&gt;
    To track the benefits after the closure of the project so that all of the value that was originally outlined within the
    business case is actually delivered, as most programs or projects have benefits that will be realized after it
    ends.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="63f0ba83"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="64b8b0b1"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="9e72f499">The handover plan typically contains the following set of information for each benefit: 
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Overview of current responsibilities for tracking
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Future tracking mechanism and data owner
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Current status of benefit realization
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Current status of benefit enablers
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Any open risk or issues regarding the benefit’s realization
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="53567b3e"></attribute>
